              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Depending on the style of the shirt (a button-down vs. a long-sleeve sun shirt/hoodie), the thin Columbia PFG (Performance Fishing Gear) shirts are called different names:\n\n### 1. If it is a Button-Down: **The Tamiami**\nIf you are looking for the thin, silky, and feather-light button-down shirt, it is called the **Columbia PFG Tamiami (or Tamiami II)**. \n* **The Fabric:** It is made of ultra-lightweight, 100% polyester ripstop. It is highly breathable, has a mesh-lined back vent, and feels extremely thin and flowy. \n* **The Contrast:** This is often confused with the **Bahama** or **Bonehead** shirts. The *Bahama* is made of a much stiffer, thicker nylon (tactel), and the *Bonehead* is made of heavy cotton canvas. \n\n### 2. If it is a Long-Sleeve T-Shirt or Sun Hoodie: **The Terminal Tackle** (Men's) or **Tidal Tee** (Women's)\nIf you are thinking of the super-thin, silky-smooth, stretchy athletic shirts designed to block the sun, they are:\n* **Men's:** **PFG Terminal Tackle**\n* **Women's:** **PFG Tidal Tee**\n* **The Fabric:** These are made of a very thin, quick-drying 100% polyester interlock fabric that has a \"cool-to-the-touch\" silky feel. They come as standard crew-neck long sleeves or hooded \"sun hoodies.\"\n\n### 3. If it is a Short-Sleeve/Camp Collar Shirt: **The Slack Tide**\nIf you want a thin, lightweight short-sleeve button-up that doesn't have the heavy utility pockets or structured collar of a traditional fishing shirt, it is called the **PFG Slack Tide (or Super Slack Tide)**. It is made of a very thin, breathable polyester blend and usually comes in casual prints or solid beachy colors.",
